      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms3u7vuir42lnm1o",
          "message": {
            "text": "The tooling-verification step exists because without it this job's whole point can evaporate while still reporting green.\n\nBoth live-render tests are describe.skipIf-gated on their tooling being present. If setup.mjs failed to fetch the jar or install Chromium, the tests would skip, vitest would report success, and the job would go green having verified nothing — the same false-negative class that made the gate necessary in the first place. setup.mjs does set a non-zero exit code on failure, so the provisioning step should already fail; this is the second lock, asserting the artifacts are actually on disk before anything claims to have tested them.\n\nVerified on a real runner\n\nDispatched against main (run 30313963004 (https://github.com/brianwestphal/glassbox/actions/runs/30313963004)) — green on the first attempt, 54s wall clock. Every risk this workflow was written against came back clean:\n\n- actions/setup-java@v4 provisioned Temurin 21.0.11.\n- The Maven Central fetch of plantuml.jar succeeded.\n- puppeteer's Chromium downloaded, and launched — the Mermaid render finished in 797 ms. This was the real unknown: a browser failing to launch is exactly how the contention bug started, and --no-sandbox --disable-dev-shm-usage is the standard mitigation rather than a guarantee. On a hosted ubuntu-latest runner it was sufficient, with no extra system-library step needed.\n- PlantUML rendered in 3.7 s.\n\nCrucially the run reported 23 passed (23), not 21 passed | 2 skipped, with both live tests named in the output. That distinction is the entire point of the verification step above: a green job with two silently-skipped tests would look identical at the summary level.\n\nLocally the env-var wiring was checked separately by running npm run test:live with PLANTUMLJAR, MERMAIDMMDC, and MERMAIDPUPPETEERCONFIG pointed at temp-dir symlinks, so the override branches were genuinely taken instead of falling through to the homedir() default. The verify step uses wc -c rather than the GNU-only stat -c%s, so it also runs on a non-Linux shell.\n\nKnown warning\n\nThe run emits a Node 20 deprecation annotation for actions/checkout@v4, setup-node@v4, and setup-java@v4. It is repo-wide (every workflow here pins @v4), not specific to this one, and non-fatal — GitHub forces those actions onto Node 24 today.\n",
            "markdown": "The tooling-verification step exists because without it this job's whole point can evaporate while still reporting green.\n\nBoth live-render tests are `describe.skipIf`-gated on their tooling being present. If `setup.mjs` failed to fetch the jar or install Chromium, the tests would **skip**, vitest would report success, and the job would go green having verified nothing — the same false-negative class that made the gate necessary in the first place. `setup.mjs` does set a non-zero exit code on failure, so the provisioning step should already fail; this is the second lock, asserting the artifacts are actually on disk before anything claims to have tested them.\n\n### Verified on a real runner\n\nDispatched against `main` ([run 30313963004](https://github.com/brianwestphal/glassbox/actions/runs/30313963004)) — **green on the first attempt, 54s wall clock**. Every risk this workflow was written against came back clean:\n\n- `actions/setup-java@v4` provisioned Temurin **21.0.11**.\n- The Maven Central fetch of `plantuml.jar` succeeded.\n- puppeteer's Chromium downloaded, **and launched** — the Mermaid render finished in 797 ms. This was the real unknown: a browser failing to launch is exactly how the contention bug started, and `--no-sandbox --disable-dev-shm-usage` is the standard mitigation rather than a guarantee. On a hosted `ubuntu-latest` runner it was sufficient, with no extra system-library step needed.\n- PlantUML rendered in 3.7 s.\n\nCrucially the run reported **`23 passed (23)`**, not `21 passed | 2 skipped`, with both live tests named in the output. That distinction is the entire point of the verification step above: a green job with two silently-skipped tests would look identical at the summary level.\n\nLocally the env-var wiring was checked separately by running `npm run test:live` with `PLANTUML_JAR`, `MERMAID_MMDC`, and `MERMAID_PUPPETEER_CONFIG` pointed at temp-dir symlinks, so the override branches were genuinely taken instead of falling through to the `homedir()` default. The verify step uses `wc -c` rather than the GNU-only `stat -c%s`, so it also runs on a non-Linux shell.\n\n### Known warning\n\nThe run emits a Node 20 deprecation annotation for `actions/checkout@v4`, `setup-node@v4`, and `setup-java@v4`. It is repo-wide (every workflow here pins `@v4`), not specific to this one, and non-fatal — GitHub forces those actions onto Node 24 today.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": ".github/workflows/live-render.yml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 62,
                  "endLine": 77,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      - name: Write a puppeteer config for the CI sandbox\n        run: echo '{\"args\":[\"--no-sandbox\",\"--disable-dev-shm-usage\"]}' > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/puppeteer.json\"\n\n      # Without this the job's whole point can evaporate silently: both tests\n      # are `describe.skipIf`-gated on their tooling, so a failed provision\n      # would SKIP them and the job would still report green — the exact\n      # false-negative the env-var gate was introduced to avoid. Assert the\n      # tooling is really there, so a provisioning failure is loud.\n      - name: Verify the tooling is present (so the tests cannot silently skip)\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          jar=\"$HOME/.glassbox/plugins/plantuml/plantuml.jar\"\n          mmdc=\"$HOME/.glassbox/plugins/mermaid/node_modules/@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli/src/cli.js\"\n          java -version\n          test -f \"$jar\"  || { echo \"::error::plantuml.jar missing at $jar — provisioning failed\"; exit 1; }\n          test -f \"$mmdc\" || { echo \"::error::mermaid-cli missing at $mmdc — provisioning failed\"; exit 1; }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
